# Cloudflare Pages / Workers-Assets SPA fallback.
#
# Every route below is a client-side route owned by js/router.js. Without these
# rules a hard request for one of them (opening a card in a new tab, a shared
# link, a refresh, a bookmark) asks the edge for a file that does not exist and
# returns Cloudflare's 404 instead of the app. Vercel does the same job through
# the "rewrites" block in vercel.json — keep the two in sync.
#
# 200 means rewrite, not redirect: the URL in the address bar is preserved, so
# the router still sees /movie/693134 and renders the right page.
#
# The explicit prefixes come first so a real asset can never be shadowed; the
# final catch-all only handles paths nothing else claimed.

/movie/*         /index.html   200
/tv/*            /index.html   200
/person/*        /index.html   200
/studio/*        /index.html   200
/network/*       /index.html   200
/collection/*    /index.html   200
/shared-list/*   /index.html   200
/movies          /index.html   200
/discover        /index.html   200
/reminders       /index.html   200
/notifications   /index.html   200
/watchlist       /index.html   200
/watched         /index.html   200
/stats           /index.html   200
/search          /index.html   200
/friends         /index.html   200
/party           /index.html   200
/profile         /index.html   200
/settings        /index.html   200

